## Setup Instructions
1. Clone the repo: `git clone https://github.com/pisanopursuit/geek-nation-multiverse.git`
2. Point a PHP 8+ server at the project root, e.g. `php -S localhost:8000` — there are no npm/Composer dependencies to install.
3. `install.php` is wired to the production IONOS MySQL database and SMTP mailbox. For your own environment, update the `database` and `mail` blocks in `install.php` (or hand-write `config/config.php` from `database/schema.sql`) before running it, otherwise it will provision against the live Geek Nation Multiverse database.
4. Visit `/install.php` and enter the database password, an administrator account, and SMTP mailbox password. This generates `config/config.php` and `config/installed.lock` — neither should be committed.
5. Signed in as that administrator, run any `upgrade-*.php` scripts you need (Universes, Companies, Brands, Events, Artist Alley, Booth/Collector Marketplaces, Multiverse Academy, Moderation Center) to add each feature module's tables.
6. Visit `http://localhost:8000` (or your configured URL) and sign in.

